      "type": "quote",
      "label": "A widespread feeling of inner emptiness, most often surfacin",
      "readingLevel": "analytical",
      "content": "A widespread feeling of inner emptiness, most often surfacing once the rush of the working week falls away \u2014 Frankl names its weekend form \u201cSunday neurosis.\u201d",
      "parentId": "mans-search-for-meaning:topic:existential-vacuum"
    },
    {
      "id": "mans-search-for-meaning:topic:self-transcendence",
      "type": "topic",
      "label": "Self-Transcendence",
      "readingLevel": "analytical",
      "parentId": "mans-search-for-meaning:topic:meaning"
    },
    {
      "id": "mans-search-for-meaning:quote:self-transcendence-q",
      "type": "quote",
      "label": "Being human always points beyond itself, toward something or",
      "readingLevel": "analytical",
      "content": "Being human always points beyond itself, toward something or someone other than oneself. Self-actualization is only ever a side-effect of that reaching outward, never a target in itself.",
      "parentId": "mans-search-for-meaning:topic:self-transcendence"
    },
