    {
      "id": "mans-search-for-meaning:topic:stage2",
      "type": "topic",
      "label": "Stage 2 \u2014 Relative Apathy",
      "readingLevel": "analytical",
      "parentId": "mans-search-for-meaning:topic:stages"
    },
    {
      "id": "mans-search-for-meaning:quote:stage2-q",
      "type": "quote",
      "label": "Apathy \u2014 the blunting of the emotions and the feeling that o",
      "readingLevel": "analytical",
      "content": "Apathy \u2014 the blunting of the emotions and the feeling that one could not care any more \u2014 was a necessary mechanism of self-defence, a kind of emotional death. By means of this insensibility the prisoner surrounded himself with a very necessary protective shell. The most painful part of a beating is not the pain itself but the insult it implies.",
      "parentId": "mans-search-for-meaning:topic:stage2"
    },
    {
      "id": "mans-search-for-meaning:topic:stage3",
      "type": "topic",
      "label": "Stage 3 \u2014 Prisoner Psychology After Liberation",
      "readingLevel": "analytical",
      "parentId": "mans-search-for-meaning:topic:stages"
    },
    {
      "id": "mans-search-for-meaning:topic:depersonalization",
      "type": "topic",
      "label": "Depersonalization",
      "readingLevel": "analytical",
      "parentId": "mans-search-for-meaning:topic:stage3"
    },
    {
      "id": "mans-search-for-meaning:quote:dp1",
      "type": "quote",
      "label": "Phase 1: everything appeared unreal, unlikely, as in a dream",
      "readingLevel": "analytical",
      "content": "Phase 1: everything appeared unreal, unlikely, as in a dream. The capacity to feel pleasure had simply gone, and had to be relearned, slowly.",
      "parentId": "mans-search-for-meaning:topic:depersonalization"
    },
    {
      "id": "mans-search-for-meaning:quote:dp2",
      "type": "quote",
      "label": "Phase 2: a moral deformity, brought on by the sudden release",
      "readingLevel": "analytical",
      "content": "Phase 2: a moral deformity, brought on by the sudden release of mental pressure \u2014 bitterness and disillusionment, once the liberated man's expectations met an indifferent world.",
      "parentId": "mans-search-for-meaning:topic:depersonalization"
    },
    {
      "id": "mans-search-for-meaning:topic:deathInTeheran",
      "type": "topic",
      "label": "Death in Teheran",
      "readingLevel": "analytical",
      "parentId": "mans-search-for-meaning:topic:psychology"
    },
    {
      "id": "mans-search-for-meaning:quote:death-q",
      "type": "quote",
      "label": "A rich and mighty Persian once walked in his garden with one",
      "readingLevel": "analytical",
      "content": "A rich and mighty Persian once walked in his garden with one of his servants. The servant cried that he had just encountered Death, who had threatened him. He begged his master for his fastest horse, so that he might ride to Teheran and reach it that same evening. The master consented, and the servant rode off. On returning to his house, the master himself came upon Death, and asked him why he had threatened his servant. \u201cI did not threaten him,\u201d Death replied. \u201cI only showed surprise in still finding him here, when I had planned to meet him tonight \u2014 in Teheran.\u201d",
      "parentId": "mans-search-for-meaning:topic:deathInTeheran"
    },
    {
      "id": "mans-search-for-meaning:topic:bismarck",
      "type": "topic",
      "label": "Words of Bismarck",
      "readingLevel": "analytical",
      "parentId": "mans-search-for-meaning:topic:psychology"
    },
    {
      "id": "mans-search-for-meaning:quote:bismarck-q",
      "type": "quote",
      "label": "Life is like being at the dentist. You always think that the",
      "readingLevel": "analytical",
      "content": "Life is like being at the dentist. You always think that the worst is still to come, and yet it is over already.",
      "parentId": "mans-search-for-meaning:topic:bismarck"
    },
    {
      "id": "mans-search-for-meaning:topic:spinoza",
      "type": "topic",
      "label": "Spinoza, in his Ethics",
      "readingLevel": "analytical",
      "parentId": "mans-search-for-meaning:topic:psychology"
    },
    {
      "id": "mans-search-for-meaning:quote:spinoza-q",
      "type": "quote",
      "label": "Emotion, which is suffering, ceases to be suffering as soon ",
      "readingLevel": "analytical",
      "content": "Emotion, which is suffering, ceases to be suffering as soon as we form a clear and precise picture of it.",
      "parentId": "mans-search-for-meaning:topic:spinoza"
    },
    {
      "id": "mans-search-for-meaning:topic:rilke",
      "type": "topic",
      "label": "Rilke",
      "readingLevel": "analytical",
      "parentId": "mans-search-for-meaning:topic:psychology"
    },
    {
      "id": "mans-search-for-meaning:quote:rilke-q",
      "type": "quote",
      "label": "How much suffering there is to get through. He spoke of suff",
      "readingLevel": "analytical",
      "content": "How much suffering there is to get through. He spoke of suffering the way others speak of getting through work.",
      "parentId": "mans-search-for-meaning:topic:rilke"
    },
    {
      "id": "mans-search-for-meaning:quote:experienced-q",
      "type": "quote",
      "label": "What you have experienced, no power on earth can take from y",
      "readingLevel": "analytical",
      "content": "What you have experienced, no power on earth can take from you.",
      "parentId": "mans-search-for-meaning:topic:psychology"
    },
    {
